Z||000000||Gerald||10-28-2001||10:22 PM||||Ok so I think I decided on a 3.8 supercharged. That should be fun dont you think  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Stupid fast. How much should I expect to pay for this engine. How hard is it to find? How hard is the swap? Im not doing the swap but Im hoping that it wont cost over 1500 to get it put in.<P>Give me your thoughts and suggestions<BR>Thanx<P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
Z||000001||pontiacs4me||10-29-2001||12:34 AM||||good choice first off, is it the series II or series I supercharged you are looking for?  I recommend the series II, although it is more expensive, it will be really worth it.  Expect to pay 2 grand for the engine tranny and wiring, and if you can find one cheaper than that then you are doing good.  I paid $1694 for mine, but it has 87k on it so Im rebuilding it first. If your not doing the swap, expect to pay way more than $1500.  an install kit from someone like ace or cwestco is going to cost you about $2000.  If you plan to stick with the manual it will cost you more, because you have to have a custom flywheel, and tranny spoofs, but you will save right off the bat not having to purchase a transmission to match the engine.  Then again, I have to have custom axles made up, and you can use the stock ones.  Its all in preferences I guess.  Im sticking with an auto, because I know with that kind of power what it is going to do to clutches.  And they are a pain in the a$$.  good luck on the swap, if you can Id say do it yourself, it will save you a bundle$$ and you will learn so much about your car that you can fix any problem that comes your way.  <BR>btw, in the next week im registering a website dedicated to the L67 3800 series II supercharged swap, that details everything to the t.  so check in and Ill let everyone know when it is up and running.<P>------------------<BR>Soon to be: L67 powered 87 coupe.||||reg||1
